<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<div>
  <p>
    Cavisson CI/CD task plugin for Jenkins. Adds Cavisson execution tasks as build steps and
    Pipeline steps, merging what used to be several separate Jenkins plugins into one:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>CavSecurityPlugin</b>: runs a selected Cavisson security scan - Static/SonarQube
    (Cavisson Code Analyzer), Container/Trivy, or Dynamic/ZAP.</li>
    <li><b>Cavisson AI Test Case Generation</b>: integrates with the Cavisson Agentic AI
    backend to generate test cases from PRDs or other source artifacts, and optionally
    publishes the generated user stories to Jira or Azure DevOps.</li>
    <li><b>Cavisson - Create Functional Test Suite</b>: creates a test suite via the
    Scenario Service REST API.</li>
    <li><b>Cavisson - Start Code Coverage</b> / <b>Cavisson - Stop Code Coverage</b>: starts
    and stops code coverage collection, publishing a detailed report.</li>
    <li><b>Cavisson - Run Test</b>: triggers a Cavisson TestSuite or Load Test scenario and
    waits for completion.</li>
    <li><b>Cavisson - Analyse Test Failure</b>: AI-powered root cause analysis for failing
    test runs using the Cav Codefix Agent.</li>
    <li><b>Cavisson Quality Gate</b> (<code>cavQualityGate</code>): evaluates one combined
    Cavisson quality gate for a build, covering whatever Static/Container/Dynamic security
    scans already ran under the same job/build.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Connection to the Cavisson DashboardServer is configured directly on each task (base URL
    + API token), or by referencing an existing Cavisson Service Connection credential.
  </p>
</div>
